SUMMARY:Teen Advisory Board
DESCRIPTION:The Teen Advisory Board gives teens a voice in shaping teen programs at the LeRoy Collins Leon County Public Library. While earning volunteer service hours\, members work together to plan and implement programs and promote them to other teens.\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n	Attend bi-monthly TAB meetings every first and third Thursday from 4 to 5 p.m.\n	Brainstorm ideas for teen programming\, including cost\, materials and marketing.\n	Attend at least one teen program each semester (fall\, spring and summer) as a representative of the TAB.\n	\n	Update the teen bulletin board with upcoming events and other content of interest.\n	\n\n\nReasons to Join\n\n\n	Earn volunteer hours\n	Plan programming\n	Recommend purchases\n\n\nApply to be on the Teen Advisory Board here.
LOCATION:Leon County Main Library
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-15236-15868867
URL:https://leoncountyfl.libcal.com/event/15868867
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261015T210000Z
DTEND:20261015T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261015T000000Z
SUMMARY:Craft and Create: Custom Wooden Planter With Cricut
DESCRIPTION:Create a custom wooden planter using Cricut in this hands-on workshop for teens and adults. Use Cricut Design Space to create a unique design\, cut it from heat-transfer vinyl and apply it to your planter. Choose a monogram\, favorite phrase or decorative pattern to create a one-of-a-kind piece for your home or as a gift.\n\n.       \n\nAll materials are provided. Participants are encouraged to bring a laptop\, though a limited number of library laptops will be available. If using your own laptop\, please download the free Cricut Design Space software before the workshop.\n\nCome early for Craft and Create: Open Lab from 3-5 p.m.
LOCATION:Lake Jackson Branch Library
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-15236-17558934
URL:https://leoncountyfl.libcal.com/event/17558934
END:VEVENT
