SUMMARY:Library Lecture Series: Florida and the South in the American Revolution
DESCRIPTION:\nTravel back to 1776 and uncover the often-overlooked roles Florida and the American South played during the American Revolution. Explore this fascinating chapter of history through engaging stories and new historical insights that challenge the familiar narrative of the Revolution. Discover how events beyond the 13 colonies helped shape the struggle for American independence.\n\nAbout the Speaker\nDr. Roger Smith is a published historian and adjunct professor of American history at the University of Florida. A nationally recognized speaker on Revolutionary War history\, he has served as a consultant for AMC’s Turn and appeared in the PBS documentary Secrets of the Dead: The Secrets of Spanish Florida.\n \n
LOCATION:Leon County Main Library
CATEGORIES:America250
UID:LibCal-15236-17563896
URL:https://leoncountyfl.libcal.com/event/17563896
END:VEVENT
