SUMMARY:Homework Hub @ Main Library
DESCRIPTION:Students in kindergarten through 8th grade can receive in-person homework assistance through Homework Hub at the Leon County Public Library. Students should bring their homework to each session. Assistance is offered on a first-come\, first-served basis.\n\nTo participate\, please visit LeonCountyLibrary.org/HomeworkHub to complete and submit the permission form.\n\nFor additional support\, students can also access virtual homework help in math\, science\, reading and writing\, social studies\, and more from 2-11 p.m. daily with their library card using Brainfuse HelpNow.
LOCATION:Leon County Main Library
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-15236-17592783
URL:https://leoncountyfl.libcal.com/event/17592783
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261019T210000Z
DTEND:20261019T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
SUMMARY:One-on-One Financial Planning
DESCRIPTION:Connect with a CERTIFIED FINANCIAL PLANNER™ professional for a confidential\, one-on-one session tailored to your financial goals. These short\, informative appointments offer clear steps you can begin using right away\, whether you’re budgeting\, saving for retirement\, managing debt\, or seeking guidance on a specific concern.\n\nTopics may include budgeting\, emergency savings\, debt management\, retirement planning\, Social Security\, major purchases\, insurance\, basic estate planning\, and more. Sessions are free. Register below\, and walk-ins are welcome as space allows.
LOCATION:Leon County Main Library
CATEGORIES:Money Skills
UID:LibCal-15236-16588079
URL:https://leoncountyfl.libcal.com/event/16588079
END:VEVENT
